  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\n\nhttps://matrix.org/docs/spec-guides/state-res-2.1/\n\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/blob/kegan/msc4297/proposals/4297-state-resolution-v2_1.md\n\n**Issue**\n\nImplementation guide makes no real mention of what the Postgres \"chain cover index\" is equivalent to in Rust-land, C++, or any other high-performance language that could achieve similar performance in memory (for a fraction of the storage cost).\n\nThis has led, in practice, to inefficient Rust implementations that bottleneck under large evaluations.",
